{
  "name": "Harbinger Direct Control",
  "author": "patrickehopkins",
  "version": "0.1.4",
  "description": "Take direct control of any champion on either team while Teamfight Manager 2's watched simulation runs in real time.\n\nGETTING STARTED\nWait for the initial match synchronization. Once the ready prompt appears, press Ctrl+Home to begin.\n\nCONTROLS\nF1-F10: Select champion (F1-F5 own team, F6-F10 opponents; Top/Jungle/Mid/Bottom/Support) | RMB: Move/attack | A then LMB: Attack-move | Q/W/R: Skills | H: Hold | B: Return | MMB drag / Mouse wheel: Camera pan/zoom | End: Temporarily return your champion to AI | Ctrl+End: Permanently release Direct Control for this match (confirmation required).\n\nIMPORTANT: KEYBINDINGS\nHarbinger's F1-F10 selection works with remapped native follow shortcuts, duplicate player names, and hidden UI. The game's native follow bindings can still independently move the camera when pressed; selecting a champion in Harbinger does not itself center or follow the camera. Check for other shortcut conflicts, particularly R (Auto Follow). Q and A also overlap native replay actions, but Direct Control suppresses those replay actions while it owns the live match. Customizable Direct Control bindings and deliberate camera-follow controls are planned for a future update.\n\nCOMPATIBILITY\nWindows/Steam; verified for Teamfight Manager 2 v0.6.2; single-player only. Native replay seeking remains disabled while Direct Control owns the live match, including after temporary End release, and returns after confirmed Ctrl+End. Some champion skill descriptions do not match their actual in-game behavior; Direct Control follows the game's underlying runtime rules.",
  "last_updated": "2026-10-03",
  "dependencies": []
}
